---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
I am an Electrical and Computing Engineering (ECE) student at Olin College of Engineering (Class of 2028), that enjoys collaborating and solving complex problems. As the Electrical/Firmware Lead for Olin Electric Motorsports, I oversee design and implementation of high and low voltage control systems. I enjoy the blend of hardware and software with a focus on software.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Olin College of Engineering"
      subtitle="Class of 2028 | B.S. in Electrical and Computing Engineering"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Received Olin Merit Scholarship.</li>
        <li>Relevant Coursework
          <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
            <li>Software Design, Micro Electronics, Computer Architecture, Signals, Integrated Engineering Design, Linear Algebra, Project Management, Calculus I, II, and III, MATLAB, Discrete, Collaborative Design</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Electrical Engineering Intern"
      subtitle="May 2026 - August 2026 at Asensus Surgical (Subsidiary of Karl Storz), Morrisville, NC"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Engineered and debugged custom PCBs designed in <strong>Altium</strong> to manage inrush current on robotic arms, ensuring <strong>IEC 60601</strong> compliance for deployment.</li>
        <li>Integrated embedded firmware for <strong>STM32</strong> microcontroller to drive haptic feedback from <strong>EtherCAT</strong>, establishing <strong>I2C</strong> communication with peripheral driver.</li>
        <li>Designed complex hardware schematics in <strong>Altium</strong>, balancing power delivery and footprint constraints.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
    
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Electrical & Software Co-Lead, Senior Engineer"
      subtitle="September 2024 - Present at Olin Electric Motorsports (Formula SAE)"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Architected a modular C firmware monorepo using <strong>Bazel</strong> for a distributed network of <strong>STM32</strong> microcontrollers, streamlining the vehicle's build process.</li>
        <li>Integrated <strong>YAML</strong>-based automation into the build pipeline to standardize <strong>CAN</strong> bus initialization across all hardware nodes with a truth <strong>DBC</strong> file.</li>
        <li>Built custom bootloader enabling over-the-air (OTA) flashing of <strong>STM32</strong> chips via <strong>CAN</strong> protocol.</li>
        <li>Contributed to high-voltage battery PCBs in <strong>KiCad</strong>, including an <strong>isoSPI</strong>-based <strong>BMS</strong> controller and 6-segment power thermistor boards for cell voltage and thermal data.</li>
        <li>Led a 24-member electrical and firmware team through the design, construction, and testing of a <strong>Formula SAE</strong> electric vehicle.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Embedded Systems TA & Electrical Shop Assistant"
      subtitle="January 2026 - Present at Olin College of Engineering"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Developed curriculum and graded assignments to teach students the fundamentals of microcontroller firmware, toolchains, <strong>RTOS</strong>, and <strong>GDB</strong>.</li>
        <li>Maintained testing equipment, including oscilloscopes, <strong>DMMs</strong>, and logic analyzers, and conducted technical tool training.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Web Development Freelancer"
      subtitle="May 2025 - August 2025"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Built a contractor website with <strong>HTML/CSS/JS</strong> that generated 185 sessions and 6+ leads within 90 days.</li>
        <li>Developed user-centric site architectures to improve accessibility for core business services.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Research Intern"
      subtitle="May 2023 - July 2023 at Clemson University Center for Automotive Research"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Created an autonomous robot utilizing <strong>SolidWorks</strong>, <strong>VEX</strong> components, and <strong>C++</strong> for precise motor and sensor control.</li>
        <li>Simulated robot in <strong>NVIDIA's Isaac Simulator</strong> to train the system for object manipulation.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
</div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Projects & Initiatives</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Embedded Hardware & Data Logging"
      subtitle="Independent Academic Work"
    >
      Designed a custom Raspberry Pi script engineered specifically as a blocking process for continuous data logging in hardware experiments.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Mobile Watchmaking Workshop"
      subtitle="Personal Initiative"
    >
      Developed project requirements and accessibility initiatives to teach watch assembly to diverse audiences, promoting watchmaking as an accessible hobby.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>KiCad PCB Design</li>
    <li>Hardware Integration</li>
    <li>High-Voltage Systems</li>
    <li>Embedded Firmware</li>
    <li>SPI Communication</li>
    <li>MATLAB</li>
    <li>Signal Processing</li>
    <li>Data Analysis</li>
    <li>Raspberry Pi</li>
    <li>Laser Cutters</li>
    <li>Pick-and-Place Assembly</li>
    <li>Git / Monorepo</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>